## 🟡 UX / Behavioral Issues

### 26. First-launch: 15-minute cold calibration with no useful score
**Files:** `CognitiveLoadEngine.swift`, `ReflexApp.swift`  
The score stays at `0` (or is meaningless) for the first 15 minutes. New users see a "Calibrating... 14 min remaining" message with a flat 0 ring. Consider shipping a default baseline and refining it in the background so the app is useful from second one.

### 27. The "Monitoring" toggle in Settings doesn't persist across launches
**File:** `Reflex/Views/SettingsView.swift` + `ReflexApp.swift`  
`monitoringEnabled` is stored in `@AppStorage`, but `initializeServices()` in `ReflexApp` calls `engine.startEngine()` unconditionally — it doesn't read `monitoringEnabled` before deciding whether to start. A user who turned off monitoring will find it re-enabled on relaunch.

### 28. Pause state is stored in `UserDefaults` but also in `@AppStorage("allRemindersPaused")` — two sources of truth
**File:** `Reflex/AppDelegate.swift` + `Reflex/ReflexApp.swift`  
`togglePauseFromMenu()` writes `UserDefaults.standard.set(...)` directly, while `ReflexApp` uses `@AppStorage("allRemindersPaused")`. These share the same key so they'll usually be in sync, but reading from `UserDefaults.standard.bool(forKey:)` directly in `AppDelegate` while writing through `@AppStorage` in the scene is fragile. Consolidate to a single `@AppStorage` or a shared service.

### 29. The right-click menu reads `UserDefaults.standard.bool(forKey: "allRemindersPaused")` which can lag
**File:** `Reflex/AppDelegate.swift` `setupStatusItemRightClickMenu()`  
The pause title in the right-click menu is read at the moment of the right-click, which is correct. But if the user toggles pause via the menu bar button (not right-click), the value is updated via `@AppStorage` — which writes synchronously — so this should be fine. Still, see issue #28.

### 30. `BreakOverlayWindow` doesn't handle multiple screens
**File:** `Reflex/Views/BreakOverlayWindow.swift` `presentWindow()`  
The fullscreen overlay only covers `NSScreen.main`. On multi-monitor setups, other screens remain visible, which undermines the break experience and lets users ignore it by glancing at a second screen.

### 31. Eye rest overlay only covers `NSScreen.main`
**File:** `Reflex/Views/EyeRestOverlayWindow.swift`  
Same issue as #30. The eye rest fullscreen should cover all connected screens.

### 32. The cursor-follower `displayTimer` fires at 60fps continuously even when the mouse is stationary
**File:** `Reflex/Views/CursorFollowerWindow.swift` lines 104–113  
A 60Hz `DispatchSourceTimer` runs for the entire countdown duration (30s). That's ~1800 timer callbacks just to re-read `NSEvent.mouseLocation`. The event-driven monitors (global + local) already handle movement. The fallback timer should run at 5–10fps, not 60fps.

### 33. `BreakNotificationPopupView` — countdown auto-dismisses but doesn't record a skip
**File:** `Reflex/Services/BreakReminderService.swift` `sendBreakReminder()` (lines 95–132)  
When the pre-break countdown reaches 0 and the user has neither taken nor skipped the break, the popup auto-triggers `startBreak()`. But if the popup was dismissed by the `breakDismissWorkItem` timeout (auto-dismiss after 30s if no interaction), no action is recorded — `consecutiveSkips` is not incremented. This means "ignoring" a prompt is treated differently than explicitly skipping it.

### 34. `SettingsView` — `showInDock` and `launchAtLogin` toggles are UI only — never implemented
**File:** `Reflex/Views/SettingsView.swift` (lines with `@AppStorage("showInDock")` and `@AppStorage("launchAtLogin")`)  
Both settings are stored in `@AppStorage` but there is no code that actually hides/shows the Dock icon or registers a login item. These need to be wired up with `SMAppService.mainApp.register()` (for login item) and toggling `NSApp.setActivationPolicy(.accessory)` / `.regular` (for Dock visibility).

### 35. Dashboard window opens but doesn't come to front from fullscreen apps reliably
**File:** `Reflex/Views/MenuBarView.swift` `activateAndOpenDashboard()`  
The current workaround (close key window, activate, 0.15s delay, open, 0.15s delay, search by title, `makeKeyAndOrderFront`) is brittle. It depends on hardcoded timing and the window title string `"Reflex Beta Dashboard"`. Use `NSWindowController` or store a reference to the window for reliable focus.

